    "rule": "br-kp1in.40 re-measurement on the v0.3.39 candidate. Written 2026-10-13 ~08:10Z, before any run of these arms.\n\nQuestion: does the v0.3.39 release commit serve fewer fetch_inbox reads (or a worse fetch_inbox p99) than v0.3.38 in\nthe release-smoke soak?\n\nArms (same build path, so features and toolchain pins come from each tree; dist.yml's feature set):\n  A = v0.3.38 tag f9c68b4e, built from source: cargo build --release --locked -p mcp-agent-mail-cli -p mcp-agent-mail\n      --no-default-features --features portable (build29/v038)\n  B = v0.3.39 release commit a4ec56bc, same command (build29/v039)\nThe receipt records server_exe_sha256 from the running process, server threads, and loadavg per arm; the runner\nalso logs CPU governor and 1-min load before each run.\n\nRuns (one host, one session, nothing else of mine running on it): unmodified tests/e2e/lib/release_smoke.py via\nam e2e run release_smoke, swarm phase skipped (AM_RELEASE_SMOKE_SWARM_AGENTS=0; the soak is the measured phase):\n  1 B_vs_A  2 A_vs_B  3 B_vs_A  4 A_vs_B  5 B_vs_A  6 A_vs_B   (3 pairs per order)\n  7 A_vs_A (null)\n\nMetrics: soak.counts.read and soak.fetch_inbox_p99_s for each arm.\n\nValidity (decided before looking at B):\n  V1. The null's two A arms differ by <= 10% in soak reads. Otherwise the host was too noisy: INCONCLUSIVE, rerun.\n  V2. Any run whose start 1-min load exceeds 16 is reported and excluded; if fewer than 2 runs per order survive,\n      INCONCLUSIVE.\n\nDecision (the bead's own acceptance):\n  REFUTED (no regression): median of B soak reads >= 0.90 x median of A soak reads, AND median of B fetch_inbox p99\n    <= 1.5 x median of A p99. Paired ratios (B/A within each run) are reported too, by order.\n  CONFIRMED regression: either half fails. Then attribute before any code change (AM_EVIDENCE_LEDGER_PATH phase\n    ledgers, focused bench inbox_fetch_project_mailbox), and the bead stays open.\nA/A crash/flow/storm verdicts are reported; any FAIL in B that A does not show is reported separately.\n\nAMENDMENT 2026-10-13T12:36:11Z, BEFORE any kp140 run (kp140d has not started; no arm has been measured):\nArm A changes from a source build of v0.3.38 to the SHIPPED v0.3.38 glibc release artifact\n(scratchpad dl2/gnu/am, sha256 171713fa43e891f8..., built by dist.yml with --no-default-features --features portable).\nReason: the source build of f9c68b4e at -j 2 on vmi1153651 was SIGKILLed at rch's 10800 s cap (build31/v038.log);\nretrying on this fleet costs another 3+ hours.\nStated confound: A is dist's zigbuild/glibc-floor build and B is an rch cargo build. Feature set (portable) and\nversion tags match. The shipped artifact is also what users run today, so A is the live incumbent.\nArms, runs, metrics, validity and decision are otherwise unchanged.\n",
